# EVONIX WiFi fragment (optional, dispatch only)
# Applied on top of evonix.config when the workflow runs with use_wifi=true.
# Brings the 802.11 stack (absent from the GKI base) plus the RTL8821AU
# out-of-tree USB driver ((CONFIG_RTL8821AU) for monitor mode + frame
# injection on adapters like TP-Link 2357:011f.
#
# Symbol notes:
# - CONFIG_WLAN=y: in-tree menu (drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig, bool,
#   default y) — entry requirement for the Realtek vendor block.
# - CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_REALTEK=y: in-tree Kconfig bool, default y.
# - CONFIG_CFG80211/CONFIG_MAC80211=m: wireless stack the driver speaks
#   through (CONFIG_IOCTL_CFG80211 path). MAC80211 select-lines pull
#   CRYPTO/CRC32 automatically; GKI already carries CCM/CMAC/AES.
#   Modules (NOT builtin): the AK3 zip ships only Image while
#   vendor_dlkm stays stock built against the modular ABI, so builtin
#   (=y) RFKILL/CFG80211/MAC80211 break onboard WiFi (MODVERSIONS CRC
#   mismatch). The workflow registers the .kos in modules.bzl and ships
#   them as a separate wifi-modules.zip (manual insmod, no autoload).
# - CONFIG_RFKILL=m (not =y): tristate with no depends; =m keeps the
#   rfkill.ko module emitted so Kleaf staging succeeds, and =m no longer
#   drags anything anywhere (whole stack is =m by design now). Keep
#   RFKILL_INPUT off (INPUT stays at its in-tree default; the driver
#   does not need RF switch input).
# - CONFIG_RTL8821AU=m: out-of-tree driver Kconfig (tristate, depends on
#   USB — GKI carries USB host). Module name is 8821au.ko when
#   CONFIG_BT_COEXIST=y (upstream default) else 8811au.ko; the workflow
#   resolves it from the driver Makefile with a fail-hard guard.
CONFIG_WLAN=y
CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_REALTEK=y
CONFIG_CFG80211=m
CONFIG_MAC80211=m
CONFIG_RFKILL=m
CONFIG_RTL8821AU=m
